TypeEvalPy
  Source : https://github.com/secure-software-engineering/TypeEvalPy
  Fork   : https://github.com/Archway-Labs-AI/TypeEvalPy (vendored via our
           fork; main tracks upstream commit-for-commit)
  License: Apache License, Version 2.0
  Used as: vendored git submodule under `extras/TypeEvalPy/`. We invoke the
           project's runner classes (`src/runner_class.py`) and reuse its
           scoring primitives without modification —
           `src/result_analyzer/analysis_utils.py` (strict scorer,
           `is_same_element` + `check_match` + `format_type`) and
           `src/result_analyzer/large_scale_analysis.py` (lenient scorer,
           `check_match` with the column/line predicate commented out).
           The harness's `archway_benchmarks.scoring` modules wrap these;
           we do not re-implement the metrics.

BugsInPy (reproduction)
  Source : https://github.com/reproducing-research-projects/BugsInPy
           (a reproduction-fix of the original `soarsmu/BugsInPy` from the
           UIUC "Reproducing and Improving BugsInPy" study)
  Fork   : https://github.com/Archway-Labs-AI/BugsInPy
  License: No declared license on upstream. BugsInPy is a research
           benchmark corpus; we use it strictly as reference data for
           reproducing detection / repair experiments, consistent with
           the corpus's stated academic-research purpose.
  Used as: vendored git submodule under `extras/BugsInPy/`. We read the
           per-bug metadata layout (`projects/<p>/bugs/<id>/{bug.info,
           bug_patch.txt, run_test.sh}`) directly from disk; no upstream
           Python code is invoked. Our `benchmarks/bugsinpy.py` loader and
           `scoring/bugsinpy.py` scorer wrap the corpus into the harness's
           native `Snippet`/`Annotation` types.

